From 806f43cbc08d88f53be284d51b577e2af64b22ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:17:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): classify draft rows with live sidebar placement
 inputs [daveey]

Draft rows used only cwd and explicit projects while real sidebar rows also
used backend project owners and known tree repo/lane roots. That mismatch hid
fresh drafts in repo subfolders, worktrees, sibling lanes and unclaimed folders.
Use the identical owners and known-project inputs for draft bucketing/filtering;
leave the existing first-send cwd and optimistic insertion untouched.

Proof: six reviewer placement probes on 43116949 give five failures and one root
control; final focused 47 tests and sidebar 81 files/1101 tests pass. Correct
invariant oracles to use all four bucket inputs. Independently remove each active
profile/connection/project-scope subscription: each targeted reactive test fails
Home->p1, while the final source passes. Hook-only probes prevent incidental i18n
renders masking missing subscriptions; actual mounted row transitions also pass.
Full TypeScript and all repository check gates pass.
